Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libsherpa-onnx-tts
Section: libs
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: sherpa-onnx (<< 2.0.1+deps2-6~)
Description: local speech synthesis and recognition (sherpa-onnx) - private build
 sherpa-onnx runs speech models with ONNX Runtime: text to speech
 (VITS/Piper, Matcha, Kokoro, Kitten, Pocket TTS, Supertonic, ZipVoice),
 speech recognition, VAD, speaker diarization.
 .
 This is the build the speech-dispatcher modules of linux-tts use, in the
 private directory /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts beside its onnxruntime and
 with the "vulkan" provider. Its C API has no stable ABI, so the modules
 depend on this exact version.

Package: libsherpa-onnx-tts-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libsherpa-onnx-tts (= ${binary:Version}), libonnxruntime-tts-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: local speech synthesis and recognition (sherpa-onnx) - headers
 sherpa-onnx runs speech models with ONNX Runtime.
 .
 Headers of the C and C++ API in /usr/include/linux-tts and sherpa-onnx.pc
 in /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts/pkgconfig, for the private build in
 libsherpa-onnx-tts.

Package: sherpa-say
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libsherpa-onnx-tts (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pulseaudio-utils | alsa-utils
Breaks: sherpa-onnx (<< 2.0.1+deps2-6~)
Replaces: sherpa-onnx (<< 2.0.1+deps2-6~)
Description: speak a text with a sherpa-onnx model
 sherpa-say MODEL [-l LANG] [-v VOICE] TEXT speaks with a sherpa-onnx text
 to speech model directory (or a name under /usr/share/sherpa-onnx/tts); the
 model family is detected from its files. OUT=file.wav saves instead.
 .
 The command line tools of sherpa-onnx (sherpa-onnx-offline-tts and others)
 come along in /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts/sherpa-onnx/bin.
